{"name":"Monk’s Cloth","hex":"#6e6355","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"monk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male member of a monastic order who has devoted his life for religious service.","In earlier usage, an eremite or hermit devoted to solitude, as opposed to a cenobite, who lived communally."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be a monk.","To act like a monk; especially to be contemplative."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monk"},{"term":"cloth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fabric, usually made of woven, knitted, or felted fibres or filaments, such as used in dressing, decorating, cleaning or other practical use. Sometimes, woven fabric specifically.","Specifically, a tablecloth, especially as spread before a meal or removed afterwards."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monk's cloth","blocks":[{"text":"Monk's cloth is a loosely woven cotton or linen fabric made of coarser yarns that drape well."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monk's_cloth","wikidata":"Q6900583"},{"title":"Textile","blocks":[{"text":"A textile is any of various fibre-based materials, including fibres, yarns, filaments, threads, and different types of fabric. Originally, textiles were woven; however, weaving is not the only manufacturing method, and many other methods were later developed to form textile structures based on their intended use. Knitting and non-woven are other popular types of fabric manufacturing. In the contemporary world, textiles satisfy the material needs for versatile applications, from simple daily clothing to bulletproof jackets, spacesuits, doctor's gowns and technical applications like geotextiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Warp_in_Progress.jpg/330px-Warp_in_Progress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Textile","wikidata":"Q28823"},{"title":"Monk","blocks":[{"text":"A monk is a man who is a member of a religious order and lives in a monastery. A monk usually lives his life in prayer and contemplation. The concept is ancient and can be seen in many religions, and in philosophy, across numerous cultures. Monasticism is historically rooted in the Sramana movements of ancient India, which produced the structured ascetic orders of Jainism and Buddhism. Benedict of Nursia is considered to be the originator of western monasticism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Christus_carthusian.jpg/330px-Christus_carthusian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monk","wikidata":"Q733786"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg/500px-Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg/1280px-Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg/500px-Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Handmade floral patterns on textiles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg/1280px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe